 To perform these tasks, we can use the functions `list_files`, `search_files_by_email`, and `delete_file`. Here's a sample code snippet:

```json
{
  "name": "get_largest_shared_file",
  "arguments": {
    "recipient": "alex.martin@bluesparrowtech.com"
  },
  "description": "Finds and deletes the largest shared file with the given recipient.",
  "returnType": "object",
  "body": [
    {
      "name": "list_files",
      "arguments": {}
    },
    {
      "name": "search_files_by_email",
      "arguments": {
        "query": `recipient:${arguments.recipient}`
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "sort_files",
      "arguments": {
        "files": ["$1"],
        "sortBySize": true
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "get_first_element",
      "arguments": {"array": "$2"}
    },
    {
      "name": "delete_file",
      "arguments": {
        "file_id": "$3"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

This function first lists all the files, then searches for the ones shared with the given recipient. It sorts the resulting array by file size and deletes the largest one. You can call this function using `get_largest_shared_file({"recipient": "alex.martin@bluesparrowtech.com"})`.
